Let's look at an example:

```java
class Animal {
    Animal(String name) { this.name = name; }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    Dog(String name) {
        super(name);
    }
}
```

The `super(name)` call runs the parent constructor before the child finishes building.

**Check:** What do you think would happen if we removed the `super(name)` line?
